course: dictionary
lesson: 8586
title: Words from history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scimitar is a sword with a curved blade that gets wider towards the end. You may not know the word, but its context helps. Look at the sentences around it and at the words that describe it, like curved and sword.
explain: Scimitars were used in the past in the Middle East, Persia, North Africa and Central Asia. You will meet them in history lessons, stories about the Crusades, and tales like the Arabian Nights. In those stories, the word tells the reader the setting is long ago.
explain: Now look at «The scimitar-horned oryx was extinct in the wild by 2000.» Here scimitar is part of an animal's name. The clue is horned: the animal's horns curve like a sword's blade. Always check by swapping in your meaning, and ask whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A scimitar is a sword with a curved blade.
fact: The blade gets wider towards the end, and its curve made it good for slashing from horseback.
fact: Scimitars were used in the past in the Middle East, Persia, North Africa and Central Asia.
fact: «The scimitar-horned oryx was extinct in the wild by 2000» means this animal had died out in nature by the year 2000.
fact: «Zoo-born oryx were released in Chad from 2016, and the herds now have calves in the wild.» This shows the animals were brought back into nature.
exercise: «The scimitar-horned oryx was extinct in the wild by 2000.» Why is the animal named scimitar-horned? | It can fly | *Its long horns curve like a sword blade | It lives in the sea | It is named after a king
exercise: Lucy reads about a warrior with a scimitar in a story set long ago. What kind of thing is a scimitar? | A horse from Persia | A type of tent | *A sword with a curved blade | A shield made of wood
exercise: Which word tells you the oryx had died out in nature? | herds | *extinct | calves | released
test: Where would a reader most likely meet a scimitar? | In a recipe for chocolate cake | *In a history lesson about the Crusades | In a book about modern trains | In a science test about plants
test: Why were curved blades good for slashing from horseback? | The curve made the blade silent | *The curve helped the rider cut as they swung the blade | The curve kept the rider warm | The curve made the sword float on water
exam: What does the word scimitar tell a reader about a story? | It tells the reader the story is about the sea | *It tells the reader the story is set in the past | It tells the reader the story is a recipe | It tells the reader the story is about the future
